<SimpleService slug="workers-compensation" title="Workers’ Compensation" description="Living Water Clinic provides evaluation and treatment for eligible work-related injuries through participating providers. Contact us to confirm availability." faqs={[{"q": "What is workers’ compensation?", "a": ["Workers’ compensation is insurance your employer carries. It covers treatment for injuries and illnesses that happen on the job, and it can include these benefits:"], "list": ["Medical care for the treatment you need to recover", "Temporary disability benefits, if you cannot work while you heal", "Permanent disability benefits, if you do not fully recover", "Job retraining or skill building, if you cannot return to the same job", "Death benefits for a spouse or dependents"], "after": "All California employers must carry this insurance. If your employer does not, the California Uninsured Employers Benefit Trust Fund may help cover you."}, {"q": "When should I report my injury?", "a": ["Tell your employer as soon as you can. If your injury built up over time, tell them as soon as you notice the problem.", "If you wait more than 30 days to tell your employer, you could lose your right to benefits."]}, {"q": "What work injuries can your providers treat?", "a": ["Our family medicine providers can evaluate and treat many work-related injuries, including:"], "list": ["Sprains and strains", "Cuts and lacerations", "Joint injuries", "Repetitive stress injuries"], "after": "Care is usually in person. California law also allows telemedicine visits in some cases."}, {"q": "How do you help with workers’ compensation paperwork?", "a": ["Our providers follow California’s medical treatment guidelines. They also help keep your claim moving by:"], "list": ["Completing your first report and treatment plan", "Completing the medical reports needed after each visit", "Talking with your employer and medical case manager when needed", "Sending work status reports about your ability to work"], "after": "Your provider helps decide your treatment and when you can return to work."}]} paras={["Living Water Clinic provides evaluation and treatment for eligible work-related injuries through participating providers. Contact our team to confirm appointment availability and applicable coverage requirements.", "If you are hurt at work, whether in a sudden accident like a fall or from an injury that builds over time like back strain, you may be able to file for workers’ compensation. Our team can evaluate and treat work-related injuries and complete the reports needed for your claim."]} />
